{"@context":"https://schema.org/","@type":"Dataset","identifier":"10.5067/J4JVCFDDPEW1","alternateName":"ALOS_PSR_L1.0","name":"ALOS PALSAR Level 1.0 Product","description":"ALOS PALSAR Level 1.0","version":"1","additionalProperty":[{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[0].Name","value":"FLIGHT_LINE"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[0].Description","value":"Flight line identifies where the aircraft/instrument has flown to acquire data."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[0].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[1].Name","value":"GROUP_ID"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[1].Description","value":"ID that helps ASF group products"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[1].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[2].Name","value":"OFF_NADIR_ANGLE"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[2].Description","value":"The angle the sensor points away from the satellite's nadir (off to the side). Larger angles correspond to imaging farther away from the satellite."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[2].DataType","value":"FLOAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[3].Name","value":"MD5SUM"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[3].Description","value":"Checksum"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[3].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[4].Name","value":"GRANULE_TYPE"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[4].Description","value":"Identifies the type of data by combining platform, beam mode type, and coverage (frame/swath)"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[4].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[5].Name","value":"ASCENDING_DESCENDING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[5].Description","value":"Describes whether the satellite travel direction was ascending towards the north pole, or descending towards the south pole."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[5].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[6].Name","value":"FAR_END_LAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[6].Description","value":"Latitude of the granule where imaging ended farthest from the satellite. For an ascending satellite, it locates the upper right corner of a north-oriented image."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[6].DataType","value":"FLOAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[7].Name","value":"INSAR_STACK_SIZE"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[7].Description","value":"The number of SAR images over the same location in the entire ASF archive. Used for data that may be used for interferometry."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[7].DataType","value":"INT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[8].Name","value":"BEAM_MODE_TYPE"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[8].Description","value":"In most cases, the BEAM_MODE_TYPE value is the same as the BEAM_MODE attribute. Each platform has its own scheme for defining acquisition sensor beam modes. Beam modes often reflect a set configuration of polarization, resolution, and off-nadir pointing angle."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[8].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[9].Name","value":"INSAR_BASELINE"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[9].Description","value":"The perpendicular distance between two satellites when they took the related two images. Useful for identifying image pairs to use for interferometry."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[9].DataType","value":"FLOAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[10].Name","value":"CENTER_FRAME_ID"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[10].Description","value":"ID of the center frame"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[10].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[11].Name","value":"CENTER_ESA_FRAME"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[11].Description","value":"The European Space Agency equivalent to the value in the FRAME_NUMBER field"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[11].DataType","value":"INT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[12].Name","value":"ACQUISITION_DATE"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[12].Description","value":"Date the data was acquired by the satellite or aircraft and instrument."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[12].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[13].Name","value":"MISSION_NAME"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[13].Description","value":"The sitenames where AIRSAR, AIRMOSS, and UAVSAR acquisitions were taken."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[13].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[14].Name","value":"CENTER_LON"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[14].Description","value":"Longitude of the center of the scene or frame."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[14].DataType","value":"FLOAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[15].Name","value":"NEAR_START_LAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[15].Description","value":"Latitude of the granule where imaging began nearest to the satellite. For an ascending satellite, it locates the lower left corner of a north-oriented image."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[15].DataType","value":"FLOAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[16].Name","value":"BEAM_MODE"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[16].Description","value":"The general type of active sensor used. Values indicate image resolution: such as standard, fine, wide, scansar wide, SM (strip mode), EW (extra wide). Or indicate resolution + polarization: FBS (fine beam single polarization), FBD (fine beam dual pol). Or atypically the type of product: TOPSAR (high resolution DEM), RPI (repeat pass interferometry), XTI (across track interferometry). Or resolution and product type IW (interferometric wide)."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[16].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[17].Name","value":"BEAM_MODE_DESC"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[17].Description","value":"Text that describes the beam mode"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[17].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[18].Name","value":"PROCESSING_TYPE"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[18].Description","value":"Indicates the type of product, such as browse, metadata, L1, complex, amplitude, projected, terrain corrected."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[18].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[19].Name","value":"PROCESSING_DESCRIPTION"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[19].Description","value":"Describes what the data was processed to. For example: low resolution terrain corrected ALOS data."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[19].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[20].Name","value":"FRAME_NUMBER"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[20].Description","value":"The designated frame or scene as defined by various space agencies (ESA, JAXA, CSA) each of which have their own scheme. The frame describes a box over the Earth at a fixed latitude. Combined with a path number (for longitude it identifies a specific piece of ground)."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[20].DataType","value":"INT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[21].Name","value":"PROCESSING_LEVEL"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[21].Description","value":"Indicates how much processing has been done to the data: L1, L1.0 unprocessed; L1.1 single look complex; L1, L1.5 amplitude image; L2, L2.2 terrain corrected image."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[21].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[22].Name","value":"PROCESSING_DATE"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[22].Description","value":"The date the data was processed"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[22].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[23].Name","value":"NEAR_START_LON"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[23].Description","value":"Longitude of the granule where imaging began nearest the satellite. For an ascending satellite, it locates the lower left corner of a north-oriented image."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[23].DataType","value":"FLOAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[24].Name","value":"DOPPLER"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[24].Description","value":"The doppler centroid frequency - Useful for SAR processing and interferometry. Related to the squint of the satellite."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[24].DataType","value":"FLOAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[25].Name","value":"FAR_START_LAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[25].Description","value":"Latitude of the granule where imaging began farthest from the satellite. For an ascending satellite, it locates the lower right corner of a north-oriented image."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[25].DataType","value":"FLOAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[26].Name","value":"NEAR_END_LON"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[26].Description","value":"Longitude of the granule where imaging ended nearest to the satellite. For an ascending satellite, it locates the upper left corner of a north-oriented image."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[26].DataType","value":"FLOAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[27].Name","value":"PROCESSING_TYPE_DISPLAY"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[27].Description","value":"Label that will be displayed in ASF's Vertex interface"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[27].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[28].Name","value":"POLARIZATION"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[28].Description","value":"Radar transmissions are polarized, with components normally termed vertical (V) and horizontal (H). Vertical means that the electric vector is in the plane of incidence; horizontal means the electric vector is perpendicular to the plane of incidence."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[28].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[29].Name","value":"FAR_START_LON"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[29].Description","value":"Latitude of the granule where imaging began farthest from the satellite. For an ascending satellite, it locates the lower right corner of a north-oriented image."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[29].DataType","value":"FLOAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[30].Name","value":"THUMBNAIL_URL"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[30].Description","value":"URL that points to this granule's thumbnail image"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[30].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[31].Name","value":"ASF_PLATFORM"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[31].Description","value":"Internal ASF platform name"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[31].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[32].Name","value":"INSAR_STACK_ID"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[32].Description","value":"An ASF-assigned unique number used internally to unify SAR images over the same location. Used for data that might be used for interferometry."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[32].DataType","value":"INT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[33].Name","value":"LOOK_DIRECTION"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[33].Description","value":"SAR imagery is taken with the sensor pointing either left or right of the satellite. Most data is right-looking."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[33].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[34].Name","value":"PATH_NUMBER"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[34].Description","value":"The path describes a path the satellite will follow over the earth similar to longitude; each path has an assigned number. Combined with a frame number it identifies a specific piece of ground."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[34].DataType","value":"INT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[35].Name","value":"NEAR_END_LAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[35].Description","value":"Latitude of the granule where imaging ended nearest to the satellite. For an ascending satellite, it locates the upper left corner of a north-oriented image."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[35].DataType","value":"FLOAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[36].Name","value":"FARADAY_ROTATION"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[36].Description","value":"An effect of the ionosphere that rotates polarizations from HH or VV or HV or VH. Significant for L or P band. Rotation over 5 degrees reduces usefulness for applications such as forest biomass. Effect is reduced at solar minimum."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[36].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[37].Name","value":"FAR_END_LON"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[37].Description","value":"Longitude of the granule where imaging ended farthest from the satellite. For an ascending satellite, it locates the upper right corner of a north-oriented image."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[37].DataType","value":"FLOAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[38].Name","value":"BYTES"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[38].Description","value":"Product size in bytes."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[38].DataType","value":"FLOAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[39].Name","value":"CENTER_LAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[39].Description","value":"Latitude of the center of the scene or frame."},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[39].DataType","value":"FLOAT"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[40].Name","value":"ARCHIVE_DATATAKE_ID"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[40].Description","value":"The ARCHIVE_DATATAKE_ID for this collection"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[40].DataType","value":"STRING"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[41].Name","value":"DEM_REGION"},{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":"AdditionalAttributes[41].Description","value":"The DEM_REGION for this collection"},{"@type":"PropertyValue",